<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>pygixml Benchmarks</title>
<style>
:root {
  --bg: #0b0e14;
  --bg-panel: #12161f;
  --bg-panel-2: #171c28;
  --border: #232938;
  --text: #e6e9ef;
  --text-dim: #8b93a7;
  --accent: #e67225;
  --accent-2: #35d0ba;
  --warn: #ffb454;
  --bad: #ff6b81;
  --good: #35d0ba;
  --mono: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, 'Liberation Mono', Menlo, monospace;
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body {
  margin: 0;
  background: var(--bg);
  color: var(--text);
  font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
  line-height: 1.55;
}
.wrap { max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px 80px; }

/* ---- Hero ---- */
/* ---- Navbar ---- */
.navbar {
  position: sticky;
  top: 0;
  z-index: 30;
  background: rgba(11, 14, 20, 0.85);
  backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
}
.navbar-inner {
  max-width: 1080px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  padding: 13px 24px;
}
.navbar-brand { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; text-decoration: none; }
.navbar-brand img { height: 22px; width: auto; }
.navbar-links { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 22px; }
.navbar-link {
  font-size: 14px;
  text-decoration: none;
  color: var(--text-dim);
  transition: color 150ms ease;
}
.navbar-link:hover { color: var(--text); }
.navbar-link.current { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }
.navbar-cta {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 6px;
  background: var(--accent);
  color: #fff;
  font-size: 13px;
  font-weight: 600;
  padding: 7px 13px;
  border-radius: 7px;
  text-decoration: none;
  transition: opacity 150ms ease;
}
.navbar-cta:hover { opacity: 0.85; }
.navbar-cta svg { width: 14px; height: 14px; }
@media (max-width: 480px) {
  .navbar-cta-text { display: none; }
  .navbar-cta { padding: 7px 9px; }
}

.hero {
  padding: 90px 24px 70px;
  text-align: center;
  background:
    radial-gradient(ellipse 900px 500px at 50% -10%, rgba(230,114,37,0.20), transparent 60%),
    linear-gradient(180deg, var(--bg) 0%, var(--bg) 100%);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
}
.hero .eyebrow {
  font-size: 13px;
  letter-spacing: .14em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--accent-2);
  font-weight: 600;
  margin-bottom: 18px;
}
.hero h1 {
  font-size: clamp(28px, 4.4vw, 48px);
  line-height: 1.18;
  margin: 0 auto 20px;
  max-width: 880px;
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
}
.hero h1 .hl { color: var(--accent); }
.hero p.sub {
  color: var(--text-dim);
  font-size: 17px;
  max-width: 660px;
  margin: 0 auto;
}
.hero .meta {
  margin-top: 28px;
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 12.5px;
  color: var(--text-dim);
}

/* ---- Sections ---- */
section { padding: 64px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
section:last-of-type { border-bottom: none; }
.kicker {
  font-size: 12.5px;
  letter-spacing: .12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--accent-2);
  font-weight: 700;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}
h2 { font-size: 27px; margin: 0 0 12px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
h3.op-title { font-size: 18px; margin: 44px 0 6px; }
h3.op-title:first-of-type { margin-top: 8px; }
.lede { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 16px; max-width: 740px; margin: 0 0 32px; }
.lede strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 650; }
.op-note { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 13.5px; max-width: 740px; margin: 0 0 12px; }
.op-winner { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 20px; color: var(--text); }
.op-winner strong { color: var(--accent-2); font-weight: 700; }

.mini-details { margin-bottom: 8px; }
.mini-details summary {
  cursor: pointer;
  user-select: none;
  font-size: 13.5px;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--accent);
  padding: 10px 4px;
  list-style: none;
}
.mini-details summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
.mini-details summary::before {
  content: '\25B8';
  display: inline-block;
  margin-right: 6px;
  transition: transform 150ms ease;
}
.mini-details[open] summary::before { transform: rotate(90deg); }
.mini-details summary:hover { color: var(--accent-2); }

.mini-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(230px, 1fr));
  gap: 14px;
  margin-bottom: 8px;
  margin-top: 4px;
}
.mini-panel {
  background: var(--bg-panel);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 11px;
  padding: 14px 16px;
}
.mini-label {
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 12px;
  color: var(--text-dim);
  margin-bottom: 8px;
}
.mini-chart-box { position: relative; height: 96px; }
.mini-values {
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 11px;
  color: var(--text-dim);
  margin-top: 6px;
  line-height: 1.5;
}
.mini-subhead {
  font-size: 10.5px;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: .04em;
  color: var(--text-dim);
  margin: 4px 0 4px;
}
.mini-mem-subhead { margin-top: 12px; border-top: 1px dashed var(--border); padding-top: 10px; }

.panel {
  background: var(--bg-panel);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 14px;
  padding: 26px;
  margin-bottom: 22px;
}
.panel h4 { margin: 0 0 4px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-dim); font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .03em; }
.chart-box { position: relative; height: 320px; }
.chart-box.tall { height: 420px; }
.chart-pair { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 18px; }

/* ---- Tables ---- */
table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 14px; }
th, td { text-align: left; padding: 10px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
th { color: var(--text-dim); font-weight: 600; font-size: 12.5px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; }
td.num, th.num { text-align: right; font-family: var(--mono); }
tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }

/* ---- Section-local download ---- */
.section-download { margin-top: 22px; }
.dl-btn {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
  background: var(--bg-panel-2);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  color: var(--text);
  padding: 9px 14px;
  border-radius: 9px;
  font-size: 13px;
  font-family: var(--mono);
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: border-color .15s, background .15s;
}
.dl-btn:hover { border-color: var(--accent); background: #1a2030; }
.dl-btn svg { width: 14px; height: 14px; flex: none; }

footer {
  padding: 40px 0 20px;
  color: var(--text-dim);
  font-size: 13px;
  text-align: center;
}
footer .sysline { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
footer a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
footer a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

.env-table { max-width: 480px; margin: 0 auto; }
.env-table td:first-child { color: var(--text-dim); width: 40%; }
.env-table td:last-child { font-family: var(--mono); color: var(--text); text-align: right; }
.env-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }

.legend-note { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-dim); margin-top: 10px; }
code { font-family: var(--mono); background: var(--bg-panel-2); padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 0.92em; }

/* ---- Major sections vs. subsections ---- */
/* A visible rule + accent tick before every top-level section title is
   the "where does a new topic start" cue; subsections nest under it
   with an indent + left rail instead of a second hline, so the two
   never read as the same level. */
section.major { padding-top: 56px; }
.section-rule {
  width: 56px; height: 3px; border-radius: 2px;
  background: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 22px;
}
.subsection {
  margin: 36px 0 0 2px;
  padding: 4px 0 4px 20px;
  border-left: 2px solid var(--border);
}
.subsection:first-of-type { margin-top: 20px; }
.subsection > h3.op-title { margin-top: 0; }
.subsection-label {
  font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .09em; text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--accent-2); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 6px;
}
.size-table { margin-top: 20px; }
.size-table tr.self-row td { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
.size-table tr.self-row { background: rgba(230, 114, 37, 0.08); }
.size-table td.cap { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 400; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header class="navbar">
  <div class="navbar-inner">
    <a class="navbar-brand" href="https://mohammadraziei.github.io/pygixml/">
      <img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MohammadRaziei/pygixml/master/docs/images/pygixml.svg" alt="pygixml">
    </a>
    <div class="navbar-links">
      <a class="navbar-link" href="https://mohammadraziei.github.io/pygixml/docs/index.html">Docs</a>
      <a class="navbar-link current" href="https://mohammadraziei.github.io/pygixml/benchmarks/index.html">Benchmarks</a>
      <a class="navbar-cta" href="https://github.com/MohammadRaziei/pygixml" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M12 .3a12 12 0 0 0-3.8 23.38c.6.1.83-.27.83-.58v-2c-3.34.72-4.04-1.6-4.04-1.6-.55-1.37-1.33-1.74-1.33-1.74-1.09-.74.08-.72.08-.72 1.2.09 1.84 1.24 1.84 1.24 1.07 1.82 2.8 1.3 3.49 1 .1-.77.42-1.3.76-1.6-2.66-.3-5.47-1.34-5.47-5.93 0-1.31.47-2.38 1.24-3.22-.13-.3-.54-1.52.12-3.18 0 0 1-.32 3.3 1.23a11.5 11.5 0 0 1 6 0c2.3-1.55 3.3-1.23 3.3-1.23.66 1.66.25 2.88.12 3.18.77.84 1.24 1.91 1.24 3.22 0 4.6-2.81 5.63-5.49 5.92.43.37.81 1.1.81 2.22v3.29c0 .31.22.69.83.57A12 12 0 0 0 12 .3Z"/></svg>
        <span class="navbar-cta-text">GitHub</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="hero">
  <div class="eyebrow">pygixml benchmark report &middot; generated {{ generated_at }}</div>
  <h1>{{ headline | safe }}</h1>
  <p class="sub">{{ subhead | safe }}</p>
  <div class="meta">{{ meta_line }}</div>
</div>

<div class="wrap">

{% macro op_body(op) %}
  {% if op.winner_summary %}<p class="op-winner">{{ op.winner_summary | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
  {% if op.memory_summary %}<p class="op-winner">{{ op.memory_summary | safe }}</p>{% endif %}

  <details class="mini-details">
    <summary>See per-entry detail ({{ op.entries|length }} corpus entries)</summary>
    <div class="mini-grid">
      {% for entry in op.entries %}
      <div class="mini-panel">
        <div class="mini-label">{{ entry.label }}</div>
        <div class="mini-subhead">Time (ms, lower is better)</div>
        <div class="mini-chart-box"><canvas id="{{ entry.id }}"></canvas></div>
        <div class="mini-values">{{ entry.values_text }}</div>
        {% if entry.mem_id %}
        <div class="mini-subhead mini-mem-subhead">Peak memory (MB, lower is better)</div>
        <div class="mini-chart-box"><canvas id="{{ entry.mem_id }}"></canvas></div>
        <div class="mini-values">{{ entry.mem_text }}</div>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </details>

  {% if op.has_time_trend or op.has_mem_trend %}
  <div class="chart-pair" style="margin-top:18px;">
    {% if op.has_time_trend %}
    <div class="panel">
      <h4>Time vs. input size (ms, log scale, lower is better)</h4>
      <div class="chart-box"><canvas id="chart-time-trend-{{ op.key }}"></canvas></div>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if op.has_mem_trend %}
    <div class="panel">
      <h4>Peak memory vs. input size (MB, lower is better)</h4>
      <div class="chart-box"><canvas id="chart-mem-trend-{{ op.key }}"></canvas></div>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% if op.has_tp_chart %}
  <div class="panel" style="margin-top:18px;">
    <h4>Throughput vs. input size (MB/s, higher is better)</h4>
    <div class="chart-box"><canvas id="chart-tp-{{ op.key }}"></canvas></div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}

<div class="wrap">

{% if has_sizes %}
<!-- ========================= PACKAGE SIZE ========================= -->
<section id="size" class="major">
  <div class="section-rule"></div>
  <div class="kicker">Package size</div>
  <h2>What you actually download</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Real wheel sizes for the current platform and Python, resolved through
    <a href="https://github.com/MohammadRaziei/pip-size" style="color:var(--accent)">pip-size</a>'s
    Python API &mdash; no downloads, no installs, just querying PyPI's index &mdash; summed across
    every transitive dependency, not just the top-level package. ElementTree ships with Python
    itself: 0 extra bytes.
  </p>
  <div class="panel">
    <div class="chart-box tall"><canvas id="chart-size"></canvas></div>
  </div>

  <table class="size-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Package</th><th class="num">Version</th><th class="num">Installed size</th><th class="num">Deps</th><th>Capability</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in size_rows %}
      <tr{% if row.is_self %} class="self-row"{% endif %}>
        <td>{{ row.label }}{% if row.is_self %} &#9733;{% endif %}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.version }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.kb }} KB</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.n_deps }}</td>
        <td class="cap">{{ row.capability }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="legend-note">Sizes measured with <code>pip-size</code> (lower is better). Deps count is transitive, flattened.</p>

  <div class="section-download">
    <button class="dl-btn" onclick="downloadJSON('sizes')">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 3v12m0 0l-4-4m4 4l4-4M4 21h16"/></svg>
      sizes.json
    </button>
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

{% if has_throughput %}

<!-- ========================= CORE MODULE ========================= -->
{% if op_parse or op_iterparse %}
<section id="core-module" class="major">
  <div class="section-rule"></div>
  <div class="kicker">Core Module</div>
  <h2>Building and streaming a tree</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    The two fundamental ways to read XML: load the whole thing into memory at once, or walk it
    one element at a time without ever holding the whole document. Time per corpus entry (best
    of {{ repeats }} runs) and peak memory (each measured in its own isolated process).
  </p>

  {% if op_parse %}
  <div class="subsection">
    <div class="subsection-label">Parsing</div>
    <h3 class="op-title">parse &mdash; build a tree from the XML string, discard it</h3>
    <p class="op-note">{{ op_parse.note }}</p>
    {{ op_body(op_parse) }}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% if op_iterparse %}
  <div class="subsection">
    <div class="subsection-label">Streaming</div>
    <h3 class="op-title">iterparse &mdash; stream every element, never hold the whole document</h3>
    <p class="op-note">{{ op_iterparse.note }}</p>
    {{ op_body(op_iterparse) }}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="section-download">
    <button class="dl-btn" onclick="downloadJSON('throughput')">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 3v12m0 0l-4-4m4 4l4-4M4 21h16"/></svg>
      throughput.json
    </button>
    {% if has_throughput_memory %}
    <button class="dl-btn" onclick="downloadJSON('throughput_memory')">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 3v12m0 0l-4-4m4 4l4-4M4 21h16"/></svg>
      throughput_memory.json
    </button>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<!-- ========================= OBJECTIFY ========================= -->
{% if op_objectify %}
<section id="objectify" class="major">
  <div class="section-rule"></div>
  <div class="kicker">Objectify</div>
  <h2>Lazy attribute-style access</h2>
  <p class="lede">{{ op_objectify.note }}</p>
  {{ op_body(op_objectify) }}
  <div class="section-download">
    <button class="dl-btn" onclick="downloadJSON('throughput')">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 3v12m0 0l-4-4m4 4l4-4M4 21h16"/></svg>
      throughput.json
    </button>
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<!-- ========================= DICTIFY ========================= -->
{% if op_dictify_dom %}
<section id="dictify" class="major">
  <div class="section-rule"></div>
  <div class="kicker">Dictify</div>
  <h2>XML to a plain dict</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Two independent comparisons, not one: dictify's regular (DOM) mode against
    <code>xmltodict.parse</code>, and its streaming mode (<code>dictify.iterdict</code>)
    against xmltodict's own streaming mode (<code>item_depth</code> +
    <code>item_callback</code>) &mdash; xmltodict genuinely supports both, so
    neither comparison is a DOM tool facing off against a streaming-only one.
  </p>

  <div class="subsection">
    <div class="subsection-label">DOM mode</div>
    <h3 class="op-title">dictify.parse vs. xmltodict.parse</h3>
    <p class="op-note">{{ op_dictify_dom.note }}</p>
    {{ op_body(op_dictify_dom) }}
  </div>

  {% if op_dictify_stream %}
  <div class="subsection">
    <div class="subsection-label">Streaming mode</div>
    <h3 class="op-title">dictify.iterdict vs. xmltodict's item_depth/item_callback</h3>
    <p class="op-note">{{ op_dictify_stream.note }}</p>
    {{ op_body(op_dictify_stream) }}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% if has_dictify_mode_chart %}
  <div class="panel" style="margin-top:18px;">
    <h4>DOM vs. streaming, both libraries, same axes (ms, log scale, lower is better)</h4>
    <p class="op-note">Solid line = streaming mode, dashed = DOM mode &mdash; is streaming actually worth it, and for whom?</p>
    <div class="chart-box tall"><canvas id="chart-dictify-modes"></canvas></div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="section-download">
    <button class="dl-btn" onclick="downloadJSON('throughput')">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 3v12m0 0l-4-4m4 4l4-4M4 21h16"/></svg>
      throughput.json
    </button>
    {% if has_throughput_memory %}
    <button class="dl-btn" onclick="downloadJSON('throughput_memory')">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 3v12m0 0l-4-4m4 4l4-4M4 21h16"/></svg>
      throughput_memory.json
    </button>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<!-- ========================= JSONIFY ========================= -->
{% if op_jsonify %}
<section id="jsonify" class="major">
  <div class="section-rule"></div>
  <div class="kicker">Jsonify</div>
  <h2>XML to JSON</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Two independent output shapes, not one: a single JSON document for the whole input, or one
    JSON object per record, streamed out as JSON Lines.
  </p>

  <div class="subsection">
    <div class="subsection-label">JSON</div>
    <h3 class="op-title">jsonify.dumps &mdash; XML string in, one JSON document out</h3>
    <p class="op-note">{{ op_jsonify.note }}</p>
    {% if jsonify_narrative %}{{ jsonify_narrative | safe }}{% endif %}
    {{ op_body(op_jsonify) }}

    {% if memory_available %}
    <div class="panel" style="margin-top:18px;">
      <h4>Peak RSS vs. input size (MB, log scale, lower is better)</h4>
      <p class="op-note">
        The streaming variant of this same JSON output, <code>jsonify.stream_dump</code>, never
        holds the whole document in memory: its curve stays flat &mdash; <strong>O(1)</strong>
        against every DOM-based approach's O(n). That's a difference in <em>growth rate</em>, not
        a fixed multiplier: no single "N&times; less memory" number at one input size represents
        it fairly &mdash; the chart does.{{ memory_lede_extra }}
      </p>
      <div class="chart-box tall"><canvas id="chart-memory"></canvas></div>
      {% if memory_complexity_note %}<p class="legend-note">{{ memory_complexity_note | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
    </div>
    {% if memory_has_speed %}
    <div class="panel">
      <h4>stream_dump speed vs. input size (log scale, lower is better)</h4>
      <p class="op-note">Best of 3 timed repeats per process, after one untimed warm-up call.</p>
      <div class="chart-box tall"><canvas id="chart-memory-speed"></canvas></div>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% endif %}

    {% if has_scaling %}
    <div class="panel" style="margin-top:18px;">
      <h4>stream_dump time vs. N, by input shape (log-log, lower is better)</h4>
      <p class="op-note">
        <code>stream_dump</code> writes optimistically and patches the output file in place once
        it learns a tag repeats &mdash; O(n) for the shape almost all real giant XML actually has
        (one repeated tag per nesting level). We also generate the one shape where it isn't: two
        different tags repeating and interleaving at the same level, shown here on purpose, not
        just cited in the docs.
      </p>
      <div class="chart-box tall"><canvas id="chart-scaling"></canvas></div>
      <p class="legend-note">{{ scaling_note | safe }}</p>
    </div>
    {% if scaling_dom_available %}
    <div class="panel">
      <h4>Records-shape XML &rarr; JSON, DOM-based approaches, for reference</h4>
      <p class="op-note">Everyone's roughly-linear time on the realistic shape, at moderate N.</p>
      <div class="chart-box"><canvas id="chart-scaling-dom"></canvas></div>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
